  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "* New: resolve a remote file's name and size WITHOUT downloading it. Added the public RemoteFileResolver helper — RemoteFileResolver.GetFileNameAsync(url) and RemoteFileResolver.GetFileInfoAsync(url) return a RemoteFileInfo { FileName, FileSize, SupportsRange, Address } from a single lightweight header probe (Content-Disposition then URL path then GUID for the name; Content-Range then Content-Length for the size). Ideal for previewing queued downloads (name + size) without starting and stopping a real download.\n            * New: IDownloadService.GetFileInfoAsync(url) exposes the same lookup on the download service, using its configuration, without disturbing any download in progress.\n            * Internal: the filename/size/range resolution is now unified behind the canonical SocketClient.GetFileInfoAsync, which the download pipeline (DownloadService) and RemoteFileResolver both consume — removing duplicated probing logic. No behavior change to existing downloads (verified against the full test suite).",
